---
import GameLayout from "../../../layouts/GameLayout.astro";
import { games } from "../../../data/games";

const game = games.find((g) => g.slug === "pulse")!;

const albums = [
	{
		cover: "/img/games/pulse/pulse_ost_cover.webp",
		kind: "Soundtrack",
		title: "Pulse: OST",
		href: "https://cipherprime.bandcamp.com/album/pulse-ost",
	},
	{
		cover: "/img/games/pulse/pulse_philly_cover.webp",
		kind: "Compilation",
		title: "Pulse: Philly is Golden",
		href: "https://cipherprime.bandcamp.com/album/pulse-philly-is-golden",
	},
	{
		cover: "/img/games/pulse/pulse_xmas_cover.webp",
		kind: "Compilation",
		title: "Pulse: It's a Prime Christmas",
		href: "https://cipherprime.bandcamp.com/album/pulse-its-a-prime-christmas",
	},
];
---

<GameLayout
	title={`Behind the Music — ${game.title}`}
	description={`The story behind the music of ${game.title}.`}
	lightTopbar
	hideBack
>
	<section class="btm">
		<div class="btm-inner">
			<a class="eyebrow" href="/games/pulse">← Pulse</a>

			<div class="layout">
				<aside class="albums">
					{albums.map((a) => (
						<a class="album" href={a.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
							<img src={a.cover} alt={a.title} />
							<div>
								<span class="kind">{a.kind}</span>
								<span class="title">{a.title}</span>
							</div>
						</a>
					))}
				</aside>

				<div class="main">
					<h1>Behind the Music</h1>
					<p>Pulse's original eight core tracks were composed in-house by Dain Saint and Kerry Gilbert. Over the months following release we added six more tracks of our own, plus seven from amazing local Philadelphia musicians like George &amp; Jonathan. We even have a track from Jim Guthrie, the legendary composer behind Superbrothers: Sword &amp; Sworcery.</p>

					<h3>Local musicians and indie talent, forget licensing deals.</h3>
					<p>Let's be honest, music is the core of Pulse. It was really important to us that we had great music. Keeping our music local (Philadelphia) and indie gives Pulse a truly unique aural landscape. If you're a fan, be sure to check out any of the generous artists who contributed music to the game&mdash;the full soundtrack is linked in the sidebar.</p>

					<h3>Using time signatures to enrich the experience</h3>
					<p>By adapting the geography of a level to its song's time signature, we were able to create a unique rhythm experience. For example, let's say a particular song has a 4/4 time signature&mdash;we'll set up the level to have either 4 or 8 rings. What about a time signature like 3/4, a waltz? We'll use 6 rings. Each pulse then represents one to two full measures of that song. This allows a freedom of form rarely seen in rhythm games, and really completes the experience. Who says you can't teach an old dog new tricks?</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</GameLayout>

<style>
	.btm {
		background: var(--cp-paper);
		color: var(--cp-dark-text);
		padding: 130px 24px 90px;
	}
	.btm-inner {
		max-width: 980px;
		margin: 0 auto;
	}
	.eyebrow {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 6px;
		font-size: var(--fs-base);
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.22em;
		color: var(--cp-green-dim);
		font-weight: 700;
		text-decoration: none;
		margin-bottom: 32px;
	}
	.eyebrow:hover {
		color: var(--cp-dark-text);
	}

	.layout {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 260px 1fr;
		gap: 48px;
		align-items: start;
	}

	.albums {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 16px;
	}
	.album {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 12px;
		text-decoration: none;
		color: inherit;
	}
	.album img {
		width: 64px;
		height: 64px;
		border-radius: 4px;
		flex-shrink: 0;
	}
	.album div {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 2px;
	}
	.album .kind {
		font-size: var(--fs-sm);
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		color: #6f7261;
	}
	.album .title {
		font-size: var(--fs-base);
		color: var(--cp-dark-text);
	}
	.album:hover .title {
		color: var(--cp-green-dim);
	}

	.main h1 {
		font-size: var(--fs-xl);
		margin: 0 0 24px;
		font-weight: 300;
		color: var(--cp-dark-text);
	}
	.main h3 {
		font-size: var(--fs-md);
		margin: 32px 0 8px;
		font-weight: 400;
		color: var(--cp-dark-text);
	}
	.main p {
		font-size: var(--fs-base);
		color: var(--cp-paper-text-dim);
	}

	@media (max-width: 780px) {
		.layout {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
		.albums {
			flex-direction: row;
			flex-wrap: wrap;
		}
	}
</style>
